				{
					"id": "tNWe1EEdq7GADy2P5",
					"name": "Kender Taunt",
					"local_notes": "Use: As a Free Action, the Kender may initiate a Quick Contest of Skill with someone who can hear and understand him/her.  The Kender uses Public Speaking (Insulting) or Fast-Talk while the opponent rolls against their Will. Kender Taunt does not work on the Undead or any creature with the Unfazable advantage.\n\nIf both sides succeed compare the Margin of Success to determine who wins. If both sides fail their rolls there is no effect. If the Kender wins use half (round fractions up) margin of victory as the penalty to all the opponent's defenses until the end of the opponent's next turn. The penalty, however, can never exceed -4. This doesn’t stack with itself or other Taunts; only the single worst penalty applies. You may try once per target per fight. If you won the QCoS by 5 or more, you may try again later in the same fight on the same opponent.",
					"base_points": 3,
					"calc": {
						"points": 3
					}
				},
